<title>JAPAN: TENNIS-JAPAN OPEN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-JAPAN OPEN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the the $1.22 million Japan Open tennis championships on Wednesday (Prefix denotes seedings):</p>
<p>Men's second round</p>
<p>1-Richard Krajicek (Netherlands) beat Neville Godwin (South Africa) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>16-Magnus Norman (Sweden) beat Justin Gimbelstob (U.S.) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>10-Jonathan Stark (U.S.) beat Frederik Fetterlein (Denmark) 7-5 6-1</p>
<p>14-Jeff Tarango (U.S.) beat Takao Suzuki (Japan) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Henrik Holm (Sweden) beat Mikael Tillstrom (Sweden) 4-6 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>6-Patrick Rafter (Australia) beat Eyal Ran (Israel) 6-0 6-4</p>
<p>5-Thomas Johansson (Sweden) beat Daniel Nestor (Canada) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Shuzo Matsuoka (Japan) beat Hideki Kaneko (Japan) 7-5 6-1</p>
<p>13-Mark Woodforde (Australia) beat Martin Sinner (Germany) 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>3-Marc Rosset (Switzerland) beat Andrew Richardson (Britain) 7-6 (8-6) 2-6 6-2</p>
<p>7-Martin Damm (Czech Republic) beat Oliver Delaitre (France) 7-5 4-6 6-4</p>
<p>16-Lionel Roux (France) beat Jean Philippe Fleurean (France) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-3) 6-4</p>
<p>Women's third round</p>
<p>1-Annabel Ellwood (Australia) beat Rika Hiraki (Japan) 6-0 3-6 6-4</p>
<p>Janet Lee (U.S.) beat Miho Saeki (Japan) 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>3-Amy Frazier (U.S.) beat Yuka Yoshida (Japan) 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Corina Morariu (U.S.) beat 7-Naoko Kijimuta (Japan) 6-4 7-6 (7-2)</p>
<p>4-Ai Sugiyama (Japan) beat Meilen Tu (U.S.) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>5-Wang Shi-ting (Taiwan) beat Karin Kschwendt (Austria) 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>2-Kimberley Po (U.S.) beat Jolene Watanabe (U.S.) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>6-Naoko Sawamatsu (Japan) beat Mana Endo (Japan) 6-1 4-6 6-4</p>
</text>
